SUSPECTED BUG: one of the two Unresolved entries has the position-less
span "-" (also as its only path hop). Every entry should carry a usable
span; the second entry, for the same variable, is at the return statement.
Deferred closure making a dynamic call (io.Closer field, one local
implementation, *spool) and assigning the named result. Under Go semantics
the set is core.ErrDropped (from flush) and dispatch.ErrSpoolBusy (assigned
by the deferred closure when flush succeeded). Deferred changes to named
results are plan step S08, not built yet (e2e origins/named_result_defer
says so), and a captured variable that a closure writes is
unresolved(memory) by design (e2e dynamic/freevar_other_closure_store), so
today's accepted result is "no Origin, unresolved(memory): load of escaping
variable err": both Origins are missing but the set says it is incomplete.
